# Standing procedures

{{owner}}'s standing answers to questions an agent would otherwise ask before a task: how
large a first run should be, which method to try first, where results go, what to report.
Each applies unless {{owner}} says otherwise for a given task. Only {{owner}} edits this
file; an agent may propose an addition (a change only the owner may approve), for example
when the same clarifying question has been answered the same way twice.

How agents use it (the intake check, in the coordinator's ground rules): before a long
computation or a new line of work, the agent lists what the task leaves unspecified, takes each answer this file gives, and asks
{{owner}} about the rest in one question.

Format: one line per procedure, under a heading for what it is about, dated.

    - <when this applies>: <what to do> (added YYYY-MM-DD)

